      ],
      body: [
        `I am writing to express my strong interest in the <strong>Solution Engineer</strong> position. With over <strong>six years of enterprise solution design experience</strong> across insurance, law enforcement, and national utility sectors in Malaysia, I bring the rare combination of deep technical delivery capability and clear stakeholder communication that defines an effective solution engineer.`,
        `As <strong>Solution Architect</strong> at <em>Vector Intelligence Sdn. Bhd.</em>, I defined the complete technical architecture for the <strong>PDRM C4i Command and Control Centre</strong> — one of the most complex enterprise integration projects I have encountered. I produced full <strong>HLD/LLD documentation, architecture diagrams</strong>, and deployment guidelines; conducted security risk assessments and data retention policy design; and liaised directly with <strong>PDRM stakeholders</strong> for requirements alignment, UAT facilitation, and operational handover. This experience gave me the full solution engineering lifecycle at its most demanding.`,
        `At <em>JuruQuest Consulting</em>, I performed solution analysis on a failed TNB enterprise project — reverse-engineered the broken architecture, scoped the rebuild, and presented the revised solution approach to stakeholders before leading the re-delivery of the <strong>TNB TOMAS platform</strong>. Defining the right solution under pressure, with incomplete information, is the work I find most engaging.`,
        `In my current role at <em>Etiqa Insurance and Takaful Berhad</em>, I contribute architectural decisions to enterprise insurance platform development — ensuring system designs align with regulatory requirements, integration constraints, and long-term maintainability. I understand how architecture choices made upstream determine the quality of everything built downstream.`,
        `I am experienced in <strong>Cloudflare Workers serverless architecture</strong> as a solution pattern — designing and deploying cost-efficient, globally distributed edge solutions that challenge traditional on-premise assumptions.`,
        `I am drawn to the solution engineering role because it sits at the intersection of technical depth and business value — where the quality of thinking determines the outcome before a single line of code is written.`,
        `Thank you sincerely for your time. I look forward to exploring how my solution design background can contribute to your clients' needs.`
